20374396, 1.1486642949748784, 7.2801896330202, 0.23026496602687985, 0.3188213789835572], "start_times": [785939.993653553, 785941.609215029, 785950.186353641, 785952.540919603, 785954.890628709, 785956.039536053, 785963.319968271, 785963.550494264], "queue_times": [0.00010780896991491318, 1.6156518930802122, 10.192784379934892, 12.547346509993076, 14.897049590013921, 16.045952964923345, 23.32638204295654, 23.556904905010015], "generated_texts": ["", "Below is a **complete, ready\u2011to\u2011run** Rust project that\n\n1. Reads the current clipboard text (Windows, macOS, Linux).\n2. Sends that text to ElevenLabs\u2019 TTS API.\n3. Streams the returned MP3/OGG audio straight to your speakers.\n\n> **TL;DR**  \n> ```bash\n> cargo new elevenlabs-tts\n> cd elevenlabs-tts\n> # copy the Cargo.toml and src/main.rs shown below\n> cargo run\n> ```\n\n---\n\n## 1. Project layout\n\n```\nelevenlabs-tts/\n\u251c\u2500 Cargo.toml\n\u2514\u2500 src/\n   \u2514\u2500 main.rs\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. `Cargo.toml`\n\n```toml\n[package]\nname = \"elevenlabs-tts\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n# Optional: enable `async` features for reqwest\n[dependencies]\ntokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"full\"] }          # async runtime\nreqwest = { version = \"0.12\", features = [\"json\", \"stream\"] }\nserde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] }\nserde_json = \"1\"\narboard = \"3\"                                            # cross\u2011platform clipboard\nrodio = \"0.17\"                                           # audio playback\ndotenvy = \"0.15\"                                          # load .env file\nanyhow = \"1\"                                              # nicer error handling\n```\n\n> **Why these crates?**  \n> * `tokio` \u2013 async runtime (reqwest is async).  \n> * `reqwest` \u2013 HTTP client.  \n> * `serde`/`serde_json` \u2013 JSON (de)serialization.  \n> * `arboard` \u2013 clipboard access on all major OSes.  \n> * `rodio` \u2013 simple audio playback from memory.  \n> * `dotenvy` \u2013 load `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` from a `.env` file.  \n> * `anyhow` \u2013 ergonomic error handling.\n\n---\n\n## 3. `.env` (create in the project root)\n\n```dotenv\n# Replace with your ElevenLabs API key\nELEVENLABS_API_KEY=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n```\n\n> **Tip:** Keep this file out of version control (`.gitignore`).\n\n---\n\n## 4. `src/main.rs`\n\n```rust\nuse anyhow::{anyhow, Context, Result};\nuse arboard::Clipboard;\nuse rodio::{Decoder, OutputStream, Sink};\nuse serde::Deserialize;\nuse std::io::Cursor;\nuse std::time::Duration;\nuse tokio::time::sleep;\n\n/// ElevenLabs TTS request payload\n#[derive(serde::Serialize)]\nstruct ElevenLabsRequest<'a> {\n    text: &'a str", "Sure thing! To make the \u201cFilters\u201d section clearer and easier to read, I\u2019ll need the current version of the document (or at least the part that contains the Filters). Once I have that, I can rewrite it in a more", "", "", "", "", ""], "errors": ["", "", "", "", "", "", "", ""], "max_output_tokens_per_s": 39.0, "max_concurrent_requests": 3, "rtfx": 0.0, "spec_decode_acceptance_rate": 37.67084282460137, "spec_decode_acceptance_length": 2.5068337129840548, "spec_decode_num_drafts": 878, "spec_decode_draft_tokens": 3512, "spec_decode_accepted_tokens": 1323, "spec_decode_per_position_acceptance_rates": [0.6958997722095672, 0.3917995444191344, 0.2505694760820046, 0.16856492027334852], "mean_ttft_ms": 116.551405415521, "median_ttft_ms": 110.3175095631741, "std_ttft_ms": 31.8724805327193, "p50_ttft_ms": 110.3175095631741, "p90_ttft_ms": 149.9452262185514, "p99_ttft_ms": 173.20582416839898, "mean_tpot_ms": 10.13713801722089, "median_tpot_ms": 9.961682291832933, "std_tpot_ms": 1.559613963896406, "p50_tpot_ms": 9.961682291832933, "p90_tpot_ms": 12.005926461195772, "p99_tpot_ms": 12.701275251459295, "mean_itl_ms": 26.12944432891744, "median_itl_ms": 26.02826349902898, "std_itl_ms": 0.8657246218584271, "p50_itl_ms": 26.02826349902898, "p90_itl_